        "verdict": "PASS",
        "reasons": "EXECUTABLE is right. Eight written acceptances at $500 from music-school directors (the buyer's own price) are on the card; 6 x $500 = $3,000 meets the target. Owner is the recorded fulfiller at 3 h per valuation: two per week = 6 h/week, exactly the ceiling, 18 h total of the 24 allowed. Direct cost and exposure $0. Deliveries on days 3/10/17 with settlement on days 13/20/27, all inside 28 days (the author waits 10 days from delivery where the card says 7, so the ledger is cautious). Cash ledger matches steps, and Brain's check has no problems ($3,000 collected in the window, min cash $0). Every chain link is established on the card.",
        "findings": [
          "No hours slack: each week uses the full 6 h, so if a signed school does not pay, the two spare acceptances can only be delivered by going over 6 h in a week or in week 4, which settles on day 28 or later. This is a risk to note, not a defect in the plan.",
          "Brain cannot yet send messages or issue invoices (SEND_A_MESSAGE and ISSUE_AN_INVOICE are NOT_CONNECTED). These have to be connected before s1/c1 can run."
        ],
